A||N||7||Seanh||Need Help Replacing Coolent Line||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||09-29-2000||02:33 AM||||Hey guys, I just got around to working on my car today. I took a look at it and had to remove the heatshielding in front of the cat. converter. Well anyany, I cant find the leak. Looking under the car, There is antifreeze on the pass. side of the exhst pipe right near the cat. I can also see fluid running all the way down to the first clamp holding the A/C (I think) line going to the front of the car, I believe the coolent hose is righ above it.? I can also see antifreeze on a piece of plasic wire/hose covering just behind the waterpump. Looking in from the top I cant really see anything. How can I find my leak? Can I start the car and let it run coolant through the engine? It runs all the time doesnt it? Even when the fans not on? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-29-2000||04:40 AM||||Might be comming from the weep hole in the water pump||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||09-29-2000||05:11 AM||||If it is indeed comming from the water pump, does that mean it is bad and needs to be replaced? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||09-29-2000||05:24 AM||||Yep<P>------------------<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New-sig.jpg"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||09-29-2000||06:48 AM||||This car should have 2 belts right? One the runs and Alt and what else? What does the otherer smaller one run. Is it the A/C comp? Also, I decided to remove the pass. side rim and the shield inside the wheel well. I am having trouble with these darn plastic screws. I have a few that refuse to come out. Should I pry them out or just drill em? Im sure they sell them at autoparts store right? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||09-29-2000||07:00 AM||||Yes, there are 2 belts.  First (small) one to go on runs the A/C compressor only.  Second belt you put on picks up crank, water pump and alternator.<P>The little plastic fasteners are available from GM dealerships.  I use a miniature pry bar to get them out.  First pry the center button out, so it sticks out, then put the pry bar under the head of the fastener and pry it out of the hole.   ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||09-29-2000||07:06 AM||||Oh geez... I feel so stupid now. The water pump in my previous posts I was refering to is not my water pump but rather the A/C Compresor. God I feel stupid!<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000007||prof bobo||09-29-2000||07:12 AM||||Plastic screws?  If you are removing the wheel well liner and/or the splash shield 'curtain' thingy, them things ain't screws, they're a kind of rivet -at least that's how it is on my 85GT.  And you can reuse them if you carefully remove them.  Get a pair of big end nippers and/or diagonal side cutters.  Now look at that 'screw', if it has a 'button' in the center, use the cutters to pry/lift that button straight out about 3/8", which relieves tension on the expanding part of the rivet and then you can pull the whole thing out by grasping behing the larger portion of the exposed disk.  Yeah, a couple will break, but you should be able to salvage  most of them.  I think you can get replacements at most parts stores.<P>BTW, small belt is A.C. compressor, other belt is H2O pump and alternator.<P>H2O pump is not TOO hard to replace, but pay attention to where the bolts went -they are not all the same size/length.  Don't forget to loosen the pulley bolts BEFORE you loosen the belts!||||reg||1
